Operational excellence focuses on running Azure workloads efficiently throughout their lifecycle. It includes deployment practices, monitoring, automation, incident management, and continuous improvement.

Important operational practices include:

* Standardized deployments
* Infrastructure as Code
* Monitoring and alerting
* Automated operational tasks
* Incident response
* Documentation
* Performance reviews

For example, instead of manually creating the same infrastructure for every application, an organization can use reusable deployment templates to create standardized environments.

A real-life use case is an enterprise managing hundreds of application environments where automation reduces deployment time and minimizes configuration errors.

Operational excellence enables teams to deliver changes reliably while maintaining stable production environments.
